1
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:04,040
Anping Bridge is also called Wuli Bridge.

2
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:08,800
It is the longest existing cross-sea beam stone bridge in China.

3
00:01:09,039 --> 00:01:12,320
There is a saying that no bridge in the world is longer than this.

4
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:13,720
Walk across Wuli Bridge,

5
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,770
and you'll be safe and worry-free.

6
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:16,840
Excuse me,

7
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:19,800
what is a cross-sea beam stone bridge?

8
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:23,320
It is a bridge that crosses an ocean or a bay.

9
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:23,920
Wang Jun.

10
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:24,480
What about its main structure?

11
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:25,880
You have eyes, don't you?

12
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,760
There was an introduction just now.

13
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,200
If you still don't understand,

14
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,560
just look it up online.

15
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:33,600
I just wanted specific details.

16
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:34,280
Leave.

17
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:36,090
Don't waste my time.

18
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:41,240
Why are you all standing around?

19
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:42,680
I paid for it.

20
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:50,479
A cross-sea stone bridge

21
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:52,200
is mainly composed of stone piers

22
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,759
and stone beams placed on them.

23
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:56,160
Thank you.

24
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:00,560
Connecting fate across the sea,

25
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:02,000
stable for a thousand years.

26
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,240
There is a saying here:

27
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:05,840
as long as couples walk across this bridge hand in hand,

28
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:08,039
they will share one heart,

29
00:02:08,039 --> 00:02:09,280
and grow old together.

30
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:10,560
I know, but we

31
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,240
have basic costs.

32
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:20,680
But that quote is really low.

33
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:22,120
Feifei.

34
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:23,640
I think

35
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,160
if that's the case...

36
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:27,890
I'll try to find a way to add some manpower for you.

37
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:39,440
What?

38
00:02:40,079 --> 00:02:41,160
I held it last time.

39
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:42,720
It's your turn this time.

40
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,079
Still you this time.

41
00:02:44,079 --> 00:02:45,160
No, you hold it.

42
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:45,640
Hold it.

43
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:46,300
You hold it.

44
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:48,200
Go.

45
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:01,440
Then does it count as holding hands while crossing the bridge?

46
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:02,640
That's not the point.

47
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:05,880
The point is today's guests are so weird.

48
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,680
If you think traveling is a waste of time,

49
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:09,680
you should wait until you have time.

50
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:11,520
Don't worry.

51
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:14,320
To deal with weird guests like this,

52
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:16,760
I have my own ways.

53
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,860
See what you two would like to eat.

54
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:23,680
Ginger duck and oyster omelette

55
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:24,960
are the signature dishes here

56
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,490
and our local specialties.

57
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:32,320
Feifei,

58
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:34,840
tell me if you're not satisfied.

59
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,560
They didn't do anything wrong.

60
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:38,620
Don't you think it's a waste of money?

61
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:40,170
It's not expensive.

62
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,300
Before we came,

63
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,880
they both told me.

64
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:46,400
Spending 1,000 on a normal graphics card

65
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:48,530
and spending 20,000 on a top-tier one.

66
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,210
Which one would you choose?

67
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,930
I'd buy the 1,000 one first.

68
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:53,120
When I save enough money,

69
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,560
I'll upgrade to a better one.

70
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:56,440
If you have to spend that money eventually,

71
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,770
why not choose the best one from the start?

72
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:01,120
Since I gave you full authority to buy the graphics card,

73
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:01,720
you should have

74
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:03,480
made the best choice from the start,

75
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:05,610
instead of bringing a normal one home.

76
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:06,370
Understood?

77
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:14,250
What does that mean?

78
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:14,760
Go.

79
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:20,240
What does this have to do with graphics cards?

80
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:21,279
It's an analogy.

81
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,880
Comparing cheap restaurants to ordinary graphics cards,

82
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:25,540
and taking a jab at Zhang Yang.

83
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:27,640
And Li Xinyue.

84
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:30,880
It's not your fault the client is complaining.

85
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:32,880
If they really valued quality,

86
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:35,280
they should have booked a high-end tour with another big agency,

87
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:36,610
instead of choosing us.

88
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:38,050
Are we not high-end?

89
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,280
But we offer great value for money.

90
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,840
But it's so strange.

91
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:43,520
Traveling with someone you like

92
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:45,250
is supposed to be a happy thing.

93
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:47,940
Why seize every chance to lose their temper?

94
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:50,080
You even used 'seize every chance'.

95
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,450
You have a sharp tongue.

96
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,360
Shut up.

97
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,000
Xinyue, go on.

98
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:58,840
Because it's a break-up trip.

99
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:00,560
Break-up trip?

100
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:01,400
Yes.

101
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:03,080
She has a

102
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:04,680
pretty bad temper.

103
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:05,440
So,

104
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,460
please don't mind her.

105
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,250
With all due respect...

106
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,340
How should I put it?

107
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:21,050
She is quite busy with work.

108
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:22,920
And most of my time

109
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,730
is spent taking care of her daily life.

110
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:27,400
So,

111
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:29,600
I don't have much income.

112
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:30,600
Occasionally,

113
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:33,260
I also help her with some work-related matters.

114
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:34,880
For this break-up trip,

115
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,340
the money we use

116
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:38,080
is all hers too.

117
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:38,800
So,

118
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:40,400
I

119
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,880
don't want to spend too much,

120
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:45,320
or it would make me look like a gold-digger

121
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:47,240
trying to make a fortune before breaking up.

122
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,200
It's weird

123
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,920
for me to say this, right?

124
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:54,400
You want the best conditions,

125
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:56,159
but preferably without spending a penny,

126
00:05:56,159 --> 00:05:56,680
right?

127
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,680
She means

128
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:01,040
she understands you want this trip

129
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:03,020
to be extremely cost-effective.

130
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:05,520
It's okay.

131
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:07,020
These past few days

132
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:09,480
have been when she's had the best attitude.

133
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:12,020
Tell you what, sir.

134
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:13,640
We will go back

135
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:16,080
and plan a new route for you.

136
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:18,280
We'll call you to discuss it then,

137
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:19,040
okay?

138
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:20,360
Okay.

139
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:23,720
After Xing Fei was promoted to project manager,

140
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:25,880
she didn't have time to spend with Wang Jun,

141
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:27,960
so she broke up with him.

142
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,840
Xing Fei is from Nan'an.

143
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,080
When they first got together,

144
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:34,000
she told Wang Jun she wanted to visit Nan'an,

145
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,240
but she never had the time.

146
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:38,040
So he suggested this breakup trip.

147
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:38,960
So,

148
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:41,480
we must make sure he has no regrets.

149
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,840
But Xing Fei could have just refused this trip.

150
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:48,040
Does she still have feelings?

151
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,360
Who said that?

152
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:51,320
Fulfilling a promise doesn't mean she still has feelings.

153
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:53,400
But I agree with what you said.

154
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:55,700
They shouldn't be left with any regrets.

155
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:58,080
Agreed.

156
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:29,060
Are you hungry?

157
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:30,540
Not hungry.

158
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:43,240
Let me make you a midnight snack.

159
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:44,180
No, thanks.

160
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:45,159
Why?

161
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:50,370
I was afraid you'd ask me for a service fee.

162
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:51,440
Or maybe

163
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,760
you ordered cheap takeout

164
00:07:54,159 --> 00:07:55,960
and asked me for a high kickback.

165
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,080
I won't charge you.

166
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,120
In your heart,

167
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,760
am I such a hateful person?

168
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:16,000
In the past,

169
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,560
I thought you were quite hateful when I disliked you.

170
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:20,160
I don't dislike you anymore.

171
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:23,640
You don't dislike me now?

172
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:26,320
I don't.

173
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,570
Why the sudden change of heart?

174
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:35,360
Are you okay?

175
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:38,240
It's hot.

176
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:49,760
Did you find the place?

177
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:51,160
I...

178
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:53,280
found it.

179
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:58,840
This is inappropriate.

180
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,140
What are you doing?

181
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:15,960
I'm sleepy.

182
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:18,000
Sleepy, huh?

183
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:22,840
How about now?

184
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,440
Are you still sleepy?

185
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:34,000
Not sleepy anymore.

186
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:34,930
Let's continue.

187
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:40,280
I might need some ice.

188
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,130
I can go get some ice.

189
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:44,080
You guys continue.

190
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:46,080
What else do you need? I'll go get it.

191
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:49,600
You guys.

192
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:51,740
Hurry up, hurry up.

193
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,160
Why are you three

194
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:05,720
acting so strange today?

195
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:10,020
Just tell me if you have something to say.

196
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:15,800
Mr. Zhang, did you put on perfume today?

197
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:22,570
Perfume? This is the smell of my laundry pods.

198
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:25,770
Mr. Zhang, aren't you cold wearing so little?

199
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:28,380
I'm naturally not afraid of the cold.

200
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:32,360
Mr. Zhang, your hairstyle looks very handsome today.

201
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:35,000
Haven't I always been this handsome?

202
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:38,160
Do you guys have something to say or not?

203
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,520
It's too red.

204
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:51,080
A little lighter.

205
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,320
Hello.

206
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:13,960
Okay, okay, okay.

207
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:17,520
I will check my email later for the offer letter.

208
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:18,160
Thank you.

209
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:21,080
I will think about it carefully. Thank you.

210
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:31,680
Of all times.

211
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:36,020
Sorry to keep you waiting.

212
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:38,280
Today,

213
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:39,840
it's really cold.

214
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:42,120
I remember when I was in school,

215
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:45,040
I used to put my hands down my desk mate's neck,

216
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:47,220
and make him scream from the cold.

217
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:50,170
Let's turn on the AC.

218
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,200
Let's go.
